decision: changes-requested

## Findings

- **N1 — medium, blocker** at [review_shim_linux.go:147](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-10750713/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:147): unreadable `/proc` entries are treated as run children before ownership or parent PID is confirmed. On systems using `hidepid=1`, unrelated processes can make an otherwise clean review fail and retain runtime resources.
- **N2 — low, follow-up** at [delegation_release.go:190](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-10750713/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:190): orphan listing uses unbounded directory reads; its byte budget does not bound empty directories or entry counts.
- **N3 — low, follow-up** at [review_dispatch.go:1104](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-10750713/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1104): PIDs are labeled as ended before termination is confirmed, while specific shim errors are reduced to a generic failure in the run record.
- **N4 — low, follow-up** at [the spec’s Technical risks section](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-10750713/worktree/.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md:103): the risk text and D1 still describe environment matching as the standard Linux path, though the CLI uses the shim. The helper comment repeats that description.

The focused Go tests and focused race tests passed, as did `go vet`. Both strict POSE validation commands failed because the read-only sandbox prevents Go from creating build directories; the sealed build and unit evidence covers those checks. `artifact-check --strict` exited successfully but reported a different change set and head than the brief, so I did not use it to establish this round’s scope. The strict surface check reported 236 results and no findings. `closeout-check` and `review-check` are deferred because they require review completion, and the brief prohibits recording an attestation.

Rules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No repository files were changed. The final draft passed `review draft-check`.

